Let the cost of a pen be $p$ cents and the cost of a pencil be $q$ cents.
From the given information, we can set up the following system of equations:
\begin{align*}
4p + 3q &= 224 \quad \text{(1)} \\
2p + 5q &= 154 \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}
Multiplying equation (2) by 2, we get:
\begin{align*}
4p + 10q &= 308 \quad \text{(3)}
\end{align*}
Subtracting equation (1) from equation (3), we get:
\begin{align*}
7q &= 84 \\
q &= 12
\end{align*}
Therefore, the cost of a pencil is $\boxed{12}$ cents. The answer is: 12
